1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
NEN

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[narrator] Nen abilities fall into
the following six distinct categories:

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Enhances are able to strengthen
and reinforce

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
the natural properties
of any object they encounter.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Transmuters can manipulate
and change the quality of aura at will.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
CONJURER

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Similar to Transmuters Conjurers
have the ability

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
to materialize an object out of aura.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Emitters can propel their aura
shooting or projecting it forward.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Manipulators can use their aura
to control objects or living things.

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Specialists possess rare abilities

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
which do not fit
within the other five categories.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
One must determine
which category their aura falls into.

14
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
This is the first step
to becoming a skilled Nen user.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
[theme song paying]

16
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
[Gon] Aunt Mito!

17
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
So long!

18
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
I’m gonna go find Ging, I promise!

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
And after I meet him,

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
I’m gonna come back to the island, okay?

21
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Bye! take care! I’ll miss you!

22
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
WISH x AND x PROMISE

23
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,000
[narrator] Meanwhile as Gon and Killua
depart from Whale Island,

24
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Kurapika is preparing
to begin a journey of his own.

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
[Kurapika] So you remember me?

26
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
[Rei] Well, yeah.
We don’t get many visitors here.

27
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
In fact, ever since you were here last,

28
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
there’s only been one other person.

29
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
This place is a whole lot harder to find
than you think.

30
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
You found this agency on your own

31
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
and that tells me you’re pretty sharp.

32
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Even so…

33
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I can’t introduce you
to our valued clients.

34
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
And it’s not because of your
total lack of experience.

35
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Some of our clients
don’t seem to mind that.

36
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
The thing is

37
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
experience isn’t all you lack.

38
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
But what do you mean?

39
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Like I told you,
I already have a Hunter’s License.

40
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
[Rei] Maybe.

41
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
But your Exam isn’t over yet.

42
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
It’s obvious.

43
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Excuse me?

44
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
You can’t see anything, can you?

45
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
[Kurapika] Huh?

46
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
You come back when you can...

47
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
[tense breath]

48
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
[electricity buzzes]

49
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
[Mizuken] You can’t see it,

50
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
but you can sense it, huh?

51
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Why did you do that?

52
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
[Mizuken] This?

53
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Oh. [chuckles] I was just playing around.

54
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
-[thunder]
-This must be fate,

55
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
us crossing paths. Y’think?

56
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Try to think of this as...

57
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
a little bit of friendly advice
from a senior.

58
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
You didn’t notice when I stole this,

59
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
or when I walked right past you, either.

60
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
You’re totally clueless.

61
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Bastard!

62
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Give me back my license right now!

63
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Does a newbie who knows nothing of Nen

64
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
have a chance of beating me?

65
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Nen, huh?

66
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[smirks]

67
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[thunder]

68
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
[Mizuken] Wanna give it a try?

69
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
[Kurapika panting]

70
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Do you get it now?

71
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
There’s something important
you still lack.

72
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Come with me.

73
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
I’ll teach you.

74
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
The real Exam has just begun.

75
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
[birds chirping]

76
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[Mizuken] Today...

77
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,000
we’re going to determine
which category your aura falls under.

78
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
[focusing exhale]

79
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
There’s something forming in the water.

80
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
So, you’re a Conjurer. It’s clear.

81
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
A Conjurer…

82
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
A type whose specialty
is manifesting their aura.

83
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,000
I see.

84
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
I was hoping I would be an Enhancer.

85
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Unfortunately, you can’t change
what you’re born with.

86
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
But it isn’t hopeless.

87
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
You can still learn
Enhancement techniques.

88
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
And that would make an excellent topic
for us to go over today.

89
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Now let’s say you have the aptitude

90
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:56,000
to achieve 100 percent
mastery of Conjuration abilities.

91
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:00,000
At the most this is how much
you could master the others.

92
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
HATSU - Enhancement 60%, Transmutation 80%
Conjuration 100%, Emission 40% ...

93
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
It doesn’t matter
how fast of a learner you are,

94
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
you can never completely
master a different category.

95
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
The further a category is from your own,

96
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
the less you acquire.

97
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Why is Specialist at zero?

98
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Specialist is a unique category.

99
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
And their abilities aren’t the kind
you can simply teach yourself.

100
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
They’re very distinct abilities,

101
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,000
either inherited or acquired naturally,

102
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
a product of your environment.

103
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
So why this position?

104
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Because the adjacent categories,
Conjurer and Manipulator,

105
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
have the greatest chance
of becoming Specialists later on.

106
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
In that respect, you still have a chance…

107
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
in a way.

108
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Do you…
remember what you said?

109
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
[tired panting]

110
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
[Kurapika] I...

111
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,000
I need...

112
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
I need enough power to fight on my own!

113
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[Mizuken] You might assume
that the fastest means to your goal

114
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
would be through Enhancement abilities…

115
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
and you’d be right.

116
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Enhancers are able to reinforce offense,

117
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,000
defense and healing most efficiently.

118
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
But since you’re a Conjurer,

119
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
you can only learn Enhancer abilities
up to half potency.

120
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
If you try to exceed your limits,

121
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
it will cause you incredible strain

122
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
and that can weaken you.

123
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,000
It could even be fatal.

124
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Consistent power

125
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
is the only way to stay on top.

126
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:45,000
If I were consistent in my abilities
as a Conjurer,

127
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
do you think that
it would that help me in a battle,

128
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
if I were pitted
against a Master Enhancer?

129
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
[Mizuken] Hmm...

130
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
In short, it would be difficult.

131
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:58,000
When closely compared to an Enhancer’s
offense and defense,

132
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
far more often than not

133
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Conjurers are simply
not as evenly balanced.

134
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
But that said,

135
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
you could actually be quite formidable,
if you find your groove.

136
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Here’s a quiz…

137
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Can you conjure a sword

138
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
that’s able to cut through anything?

139
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
You can’t.

140
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,000
[Mizuken] Why not?

141
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Because it exceeds
the bounds of human capacity.

142
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
That’s exactly right.

143
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
There are things you can never conjure,

144
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
even with 100 percent mastery.

145
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Of course,

146
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
you could conjure a sword
that’s very sharp and sturdy.

147
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,000
But it would make a lot more sense
to just go out and buy one.

148
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
You wouldn’t need extra training.

149
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,000
You can make the sword
appear and disappear using Nen.

150
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
But conjured weapons
just aren’t as effective.

151
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
The physical versions are better.

152
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Unfortunately,

153
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
you can’t conjure anything
that’s supernatural.

154
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
So, consider it carefully

155
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
and choose what you wish to conjure.

156
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
No mistakes allowed.

157
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Conjuring something at will
takes a lot of concentration,

158
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
not to mention training and time.

159
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
And that’s just what it takes

160
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
for one thing.

161
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
[Rei] What a surprise…

162
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[Kurapika] Huh?

163
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:18,000
I don’t know many people
who learned Nen in only six months.

164
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
So. What kind of employer do you want?

165
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
I’ll tell you something interesting
about spiders…

166
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Meet me in Yorknew City on September 1st.

167
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
I would prefer to find an employer

168
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
with strong ties to the Yorknew Auction.

169
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
The job is irrelevant.

170
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
[Rei] The Yorknew City auction…

171
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
The employers who have a lot of influence,

172
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
generally post the difficult jobs.

173
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
I doubt they’re looking to hire a Hunter
with zero experience.

174
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
I see three.

175
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Three employers who’ll decide

176
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
based on the interview
and not on your record.

177
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
And it looks like all three
are looking for bodyguards.

178
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
I’ll read, you choose, ‘k?

179
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,000
The first is a handgun buff.

180
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:18,000
He’s after the Misette Limited Edition
Bull Snake Model S55,

181
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,000
number 001.

182
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
The second is a collector of fine china.

183
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
This one is seeking Rodo Memorial Plates

184
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,000
from 1655 to 1657.

185
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
And the third…

186
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
is a flesh collector...

187
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Seeking a hide with a full body tattoo
of a rising dragon,

188
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:42,000
the head of a child with Jelly Syndrome
and a few others.

189
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
That sure is quite a hobby.

190
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
All right. Take your pick.

191
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Huh?

192
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
[Mizuken] Chains?

193
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
[Kurapika]
Yes. When you said I was a Conjurer,

194
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
that was the first thing
that came to mind.

195
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Interesting.

196
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
But why chains?

197
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:03,000
It’s because there are some people
at large in the world right now,

198
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
who need to be chained to hell.

199
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Oh, is that so?

200
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Because I can’t shake
the nagging suspicion

201
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
that you’re the one
who’ll be chained down.

202
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[Kurapika] What the hell do you know?

203
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Wait a second! Where are you going?

204
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
I’m your teacher! Do as I say!

205
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
I’m not done talking to you!

206
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Hold on, dammit!

207
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Like I told you ordinary chains
are pointless!

208
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
They’re inferior!

209
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
And conjuring
some kind of unbreakable chain

210
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
is completely impossible!

211
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
[Kurapika] On September 1st,

212
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Yorknew City will host

213
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
the world’s greatest auction.

214
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
That’s where the spider…

215
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,000
the Phantom Troupe will appear.

216
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
[chains jangling]

217
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Huh?

218
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
That heartbeat…

219
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
It plays a horrible melody of rage…

220
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
So, you want me to find you an employer

221
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
with connections to the Yorknew auction?

222
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Did I get that right?

223
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
That’s right.

224
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Like the last guy who walked in.

225
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Huh?

226
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Same request twice today.

227
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Amusing, is all.

228
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
The boy I just passed?

229
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
[Rei] Do you know him?

230
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
No, I don’t.

231
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
He’s interested in the auction, too?

232
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,000
But then…

233
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
why is his heartbeat so full of rage?

234
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:56,000
RITZ-CARLTON HOTEL

235
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
[cringing]

236
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
[thug 1] Eating with a twerp like that’ll
only make your food taste worse.

237
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
[thug 2]
Why don’t you let us take you out instead?

238
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
We’ll show you
the best night of your life, sweetheart.

239
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
This isn’t a date, unfortunately.

240
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
I’m in the middle of a job.

241
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
A job? Really?

242
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
-[man cringing]
-This is actually my employer.

243
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
He’s hired me as his bodyguard.

244
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
[thug 1] Bodyguard?

245
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
[thug 2] You’ve gotta be joking.

246
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
A babe like you… a bodyguard?

247
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
[all thugs laughing]

248
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
I’d be happy to let you guard my body…

249
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
I don't guard ugly men.

250
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
But thanks anyway.

251
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Who do you think you’re talkin’ to?

252
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Shut your--

253
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
[pervy cackle]

254
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[woman] Instant Lover.

255
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
180-MINUTE LOVE SLAVE
INSTANT LOVER

256
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Every single person that I kiss

257
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
becomes my willing slave.

258
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,000
[panting]

259
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
What’s your command, mistress?

260
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
I live to serve you!

261
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Beat them up for me.

262
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Yes, ma’am! My pleasure!

263
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
[all three thugs] Huh?

264
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
[gleeful laughter]

265
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
[punches and grunting]

266
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
[frightened squeak]

267
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[screaming in terror]

268
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
[tires screeching]

269
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
[annoyed grunt] He ran away.

270
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Ah, well.
Guess I’ll need another employer.

271
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,000
What a pain…

272
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
A splendid moon…

273
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
[guard 1] There he is!

274
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[guard 2] We’ve got you now!

275
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
[guard 3] Hand over the corpse samples
you stole, nice and easy!

276
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[derisive snort]

277
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Don’t interrupt.

278
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Not my work and not this splendid moon.

279
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,000
[annoyed growl]

280
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
That’s enough! Put your hands up!

281
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[Basho] I was on the verge
of another masterful poem.

282
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
But you spoiled the moment, you imbeciles!

283
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
“Splendid full moon

284
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
and pursuers as clumsy as a baboon…”

285
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
[grunts] That sucks.

286
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,000
[birds chirping]

287
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
[Squala] Yes, I know, Eliza.

288
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Well, if this job works out…

289
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Yeah. There’s nothing to worry about.

290
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,000
I’ll handle it.

291
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Right. I’ll take care of you and the dogs.

292
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Really won’t be a problem.

293
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
So, don’t worry, Eliza.

294
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Bear with me a little while longer.

295
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Yeah. It’ll be fine.

296
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
You can count on me.

297
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
[doorbell sounds]

298
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[Kurapika]
I was sent by the employment agency.

299
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
My name is Kurapika.

300
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
[dogs growling]

301
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Welcome.
We’re happy that you could join us.

302
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
If you’d be so kind as to wait here.

303
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
[butler] Thank you for your patience.

304
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,000
It seems everyone has arrived,

305
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:23,000
so we will now begin
going over the details of the contract.

306
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,000
I’ll start by going over the requirements.

307
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
I won’t ask whether or not

308
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
you have a License.

309
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,000
My only concern

310
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
is whether you can obtain
the items we seek.

311
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
The auction, as you all know,

312
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,000
will begin in one month.

313
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Before that time,
find one item from the list provided

314
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
and then bring it safely back here.

315
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Here you go.

316
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
These are the data cards you’re assigned.

317
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,000
LOCK OF HAIR FROM THE FAMOUS ACTRESS, SARA

318
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
A RIGHT ARM OF A MUMMY
FROM AN EGYPTIAN TOMB

319
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
THE SCALY SKIN OF A PATIENT
WITH ICHTHYOSIS

320
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,000
THE SKULL OF A ONE-HORNED CREATURE

321
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
[gasps]

322
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:21,000
THE EYEBALLS OF A KURTA.

323
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
[seething]

324
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,000
What?

325
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Something wrong?
You look a little pale.

326
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Ah. The eyeballs of a Kurta, huh?

327
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
“Difficulty Level: A.

328
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Preserve the post-mortem scarlet hue
after death.

329
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Complete set with head preferred."

330
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Yeah, I’ve heard about that.

331
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Their eyes turn red
whenever they’re excited.

332
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
-You see, the Kurta--
-Shut up.

333
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
That’s enough.

334
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,000
[derisive snort]

335
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
I'll say it again:

336
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
All that’s required is one item
from the list you’ve been given.

337
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,000
If you are successful,

338
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
you’ll be hired

339
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:07,000
and begin your training
in security and acquisitions.

340
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Well, then. Best of luck to you.

341
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
[Kurapika] I will pass this test.

342
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
First, I must ingratiate myself
and win their trust.

343
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:22,000
In all likelihood, the man we saw
was not the actual client,

344
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
thus, illustrating the distance
between the client and myself.

345
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
It’s critical that I get
as close to them as possible

346
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
until they eventually let their guard down
and share their secrets.

347
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
There are two things
that collectors always desire.

348
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
The first is any item of extreme rarity.

349
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
The second is colleagues to whom
they can brag about their collection.

350
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
He must have connections
to other flesh collectors...

351
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
those who share
their disgusting acquisitions,

352
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
a network of scum.

353
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
I will infiltrate their ranks

354
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,000
and eradicate them all.

355
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
[mustached man] Hey… It won’t open.

356
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
[man on screen]
I forgot to mention one thing:

357
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:12,000
the minimum requirement for the position
is strength.

358
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Enough strength
to get out of this mansion...

359
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
with your lives.

360
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
[narrator] Kurapika pursues his quest

361
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
to avenge his brethren
and punish the Phantom Troupe.

362
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:43,000
And right now,

363
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
he is preparing
to enter a new battlefield.

364
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:51,000
[theme song playing]

365
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
[Gon] Coming up:

366
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

367
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

368
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

369
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

370
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Today we’re introducing Mizuken,
Kurapika’s teacher!

371
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
And he’s an Emitter type.

372
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
I guess Nen users are fated
to meet Nen teachers.

373
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,000
It happened to us.

374
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:15,000
[both] Maybe that’s why we met each other.
It’s fate!

375
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon] Next Time: "Nen x Users x Unite"?

376
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Killua] Hey, Gon…

377
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Let's go break
some of Milluki's figurines!

378
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Gon] Count me in as your accomplice!
